(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// sys.settrace (queue 219t; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 219t\"): the legacy tracer as sys.monitoring's tool 7"] [4 1 "// (PY_MONITORING_SYS_TRACE_ID), beside 220's profiler (tool 6, monitoring.go), as CPython 3.14.10's"] [5 1 "// Python/legacy_tracing.c makes it (PSF License Agreement): PY_START, PY_RESUME and PY_THROW are 'call', PY_RETURN and"] [6 1 "// PY_YIELD 'return' with the value, PY_UNWIND 'return' with None, RAISE 'exception' with (type, value, traceback); the"] [7 1 "// local events LINE (and the legacy JUMP and INSTRUCTION: a backward jump's 'line', 'opcode') from the dispatch loop"] [8 1 "// (traceInstr), by Python/instrumentation.c's rule over pyi's IR (initialize_lines, _Py_call_instrumentation_line). The"] [9 1 "// trampoline is Python/sysmodule.c's trace_trampoline. f_lineno's jumps are Objects/frameobject.c's"] [10 1 "// frame_lineno_set_impl over mark_stacks, ported to pyi's IR."] [11 1 "//"] [12 1 "// While a trace function is set (or a tool has LINE, INSTRUCTION or JUMP events: monTraceMask), frames run on the loop:"] [13 1 "// guardedStep and step enter a code object's compiled body only when tracing is off, and a compiled frame already"] [14 1 "// running returns AotToLoop at its next block start (arbace.python.aot's check, AotTracing), its whole stack in the"] [15 1 "// frame, guardedStep continuing it on the loop."] [17 1 "// the events' numbers beyond monitoring.go's"] [23 2 "// monTraceTool is the legacy tracer's tool (PY_MONITORING_SYS_TRACE_ID)"] [25 2 "// monTraceMask are the events the loop reports: while one is set no frame runs compiled"] [27 2 "// traceEvents are the legacy tracer's (legacy_tracing.c's _PyEval_SetTrace less STOP_ITERATION)"] [33 2 "// traceFuncs are the threads' trace functions (tstate->c_traceobj)"] [35 2 "// traceWhat is the event of the trace function a thread runs (tstate->what_event), absent when none: f_lineno's"] [36 2 "// setter reads it"] [40 1 "// AotToLoop is a compiled body's answer at a block start while tracing (queue 219t): f.PC is the block start, the whole"] [41 1 "// value stack in f.Stack; guardedStep runs the frame on the loop from there."] [48 1 "// AotTracing is whether frames must run on the loop (a trace function or a line tool set): the compiled code's check"] [49 1 "// at each block start and after each direct call."] [62 1 "// setTrace is _PyEval_SetTrace for t: fn None removes it."] [72 1 "// traceCall is trace_trampoline: the 'call' event to the thread's trace function, the others to f's f_trace; a result"] [73 1 "// other than None becomes f_trace; an error removes the trace function and f_trace and is returned."] [112 1 "// traceEvent is the legacy tracer's callback for the frame events (monFire's native)."] [136 1 "// monRaise is RAISE at f (runFrames, where the frame's traceback entry is added: CPython's monitor_raise at its error"] [137 1 "// label, not at a re-raise); a callback's error replaces the exception."] [148 1 "// traceLines are c's instructions that may start a line event (initialize_lines): a line different from the previous"] [149 1 "// instruction's in code order, a jump's target, a handler's target; never the RESUME nop at 0."] [184 1 "// resumeAt0 is whether c starts with its RESUME, the nop arbace.python.compile puts at co_firstlineno (a module has none)."] [189 1 "// traceInstr is the loop's hook before f runs instruction f.PC while tracing: the line event (a line's instrumented"] [190 1 "// instruction reached from another line, or after a RESUME: the frame's start, a resumption after a yield), the opcode"] [191 1 "// event, a backward jump's line event. A trace function's jump (f_lineno) changes f.PC: the target then runs with no"] [192 1 "// event of its own. An error is raised at the instruction."] [254 1 "// monLocal fires a loop event ev to the tools but the legacy tracer that registered it."] [273 1 "// f_lineno's jumps: the kinds of mark_stacks' slots, three bits each in an int64 (the top the low bits)"] [319 1 "// irEffect is instruction in's stack effect falling through and jumping (arbace.python.ir's table)."] [376 1 "// markStacks is mark_stacks over c's IR: each instruction's stack as its slots' kinds, stackUninit where unreached."] [495 1 "// frameSetLineno is frame_lineno_set_impl: a jump to line v from a trace function's event."] [524 2 "// marklines: each line's first instruction in code order"] [594 24 "// the value the yield popped"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[91 20] [119 35] [139 76] [140 29] [170 21] [176 24] [216 51] [221 79] [229 58] [234 86] [241 50] [246 103] [263 21] [350 13] [350 21] [389 18] [389 24] [391 13] [391 20] [426 9] [426 16] [429 9] [429 16] [497 22] [527 12] [527 19] [529 20] [548 12] [548 19] [584 103]]} (go/file "trace.go" :imports [])

;; sys.settrace (queue 219t; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "Design: 219t"): the legacy tracer as sys.monitoring's tool 7
;; (PY_MONITORING_SYS_TRACE_ID), beside 220's profiler (tool 6, monitoring.go), as CPython 3.14.10's
;; Python/legacy_tracing.c makes it (PSF License Agreement): PY_START, PY_RESUME and PY_THROW are 'call', PY_RETURN and
;; PY_YIELD 'return' with the value, PY_UNWIND 'return' with None, RAISE 'exception' with (type, value, traceback); the
;; local events LINE (and the legacy JUMP and INSTRUCTION: a backward jump's 'line', 'opcode') from the dispatch loop
;; (traceInstr), by Python/instrumentation.c's rule over pyi's IR (initialize_lines, _Py_call_instrumentation_line). The
;; trampoline is Python/sysmodule.c's trace_trampoline. f_lineno's jumps are Objects/frameobject.c's
;; frame_lineno_set_impl over mark_stacks, ported to pyi's IR.
;;
;; While a trace function is set (or a tool has LINE, INSTRUCTION or JUMP events: monTraceMask), frames run on the loop:
;; guardedStep and step enter a code object's compiled body only when tracing is off, and a compiled frame already
;; running returns AotToLoop at its next block start (arbace.python.aot's check, AotTracing), its whole stack in the
;; frame, guardedStep continuing it on the loop.


